State("DASHATTACK2")
{
Posture("Stand");
Animation("stand_dashattack")
{
AimType("FullBody");
BlendInTime(0.10);
BlendOutTime(0.25);
BlendTimeTo("stand_attack1c", 0.4);
}
to this:
State("DASHATTACK2")
{
Posture("Stand");
Animation("stand_dashattack")
{
AimType("FullBody");
BlendInTime(0.10);
BlendOutTime(0.25);
BlendTimeTo("stand_gam_guard", 0.4);
}
Your first tip should be that you're trying to reference an animation that doesn't exist - however, the reason you not only change the animation but
move the state as well
is because that animation hasn't been declared (animations need to be declared before they can be referenced in BlendTimes).

