1) That's going to be the result of cockpit tension. There's an odf parameter for it, try playing around with it.\n2) Like vampire_lord said, not without smoothing your terrain out. If the terrain is too sheer, you're out of luck. (Or you could use objects for collision, but usually when terrain is sheer enough to lose collision it looks bad anyway.)\n3) You need three separate functions for your regions, you can't combine them like you did.\nCode:\nSelect all\nOnEnterRegion(
function(regIn,character)
MoveEntityToNode(character,"TeleportNode")
end,
"TeleportRegion")
ActivateRegion("TeleportRegion")

OnEnterRegion(
function(regIn,character)
MoveEntityToNode(character,"cis_telepath")
end,
"cis-tele")
ActivateRegion("cis-tele")

OnEnterRegion(
function(regIn,character)
MoveEntityToNode(character,"Snipernode")
end,
"TeleportSniper")
ActivateRegion("TeleportSniper")\nMake sure you read through the scripting system doc and take a look at campaign luas to get an idea of how to actually work with functions.\n4) Since we can't see your .lua, it's hard to tell, but likely there's something wrong in the way you set up your sound worlds folder. Tell you what, send me your .lua and your sound worlds folder in a .zip and I'll take a look at it and let you know what you did wrong (or you could just follow my guide carefully).\n5) Again, scripting_system.doc. It's in the documentation folder in your ModTools.

